        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">You cannot really run on a standard walking pad, and you can only
            lightly jog on a 2-in-1.</strong> Flat pads top out around a brisk walk; 2-in-1 pads with
            the rail raised commonly reach about 6 mph. In both cases the short belt, small motor and
            missing frame make running a poor fit and a faster route to wear, overheating and falls.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you want to run, buy a treadmill with a belt of 55 to 60 inches, a continuous motor
            rating, full rails and a safety clip — a folding model if space is tight. If you want to
            walk, a pad does that well. Our guide to the
